# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on Windows as well. Three checks in
# this repository compare a generated file with the copy that is committed --
# crates/stylex-rs-compiler/parity/corpus/harvested.json,
# crates/postcss-value-parser/src/tests/cases.rs and
# crates/stylex-utils/src/tests/number_parse_float_cases.rs -- and Git for
# Windows checks text out as CRLF by default, which fails all three while the
# content is identical. Git decides what is text by content, so binary files
# are untouched. The checks do not rely on this rule alone. The harvest check
# reads through a documented reader, the two `diff` checks pass
# `--strip-trailing-cr`, and scripts/git/lib/generated-fixtures.mjs holds them
# to it.
* text=auto eol=lf

